SUMMARY:🌟 A Course in Miracles Study Group
DESCRIPTION:Center for Spiritual Living Asheville\n**A Course In Miracles 
 Study Group**\n\n*✨ All are welcome to join us for A Course in Miracles 
 at the Center for Spiritual Living Asheville!*\n\n📅 When: First & Third
  Fridays of each month\n🕐 Time: 1:00 PM – 2:30 PM\n💜 Love Offering
  to support the Community\n\n**🌟 About Our Gatherings**\n🃏 During ea
 ch meeting\, we each choose a card from the "Miracle Cards" — inviting S
 pirit to guide us to exactly the right message for ourselves or the group 
 in that moment.\n📖 When time allows\, we also share a lesson from the W
 orkbook together.\n🚪 You are welcome to join at any time — no need to
  start from the beginning!\n\n**💡 New to ACIM? Here's the heart of it:*
 *\nA miracle is a shift in perception from fear to Love.\n"Nothing real ca
 n be threatened\, nothing unreal exists — therein lies the peace of God.
 "\n\n☮️ Come join us for some POG (Peace of God)!\n\n🙏 Wishing you 
 a year filled with Miracles\, Love & Light!\n\nWith love\,\nMarla (Facilit
 ator) & Robin (Co-Facilitator)\n\n#ACourseInMiracles #ACIM #PeaceOfGod #Sp
 iritualLiving #CSLAsheville #CommunityCommons #MiracleCards #ShiftInPercep
 tion #LoveAndLight #Miracles #SpiritualGrowth #Asheville #AshevilleEvents 
 #MindfulCommunity #InnerPeace
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/center-for-spiritual-living-asheville
 /events/vwlvbvyjcpbbc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261030T183601Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030T183601Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/beg-botany-nov-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T160000
DTSTAMP:20261002T215543Z
CREATED:20261002T215543Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T215543Z
UID:1778780020234-1795179600-1795190400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Beginning Botany
DESCRIPTION:Beginning Botany\nwith Alexandra Holland \nFriday\, November 20  |  1 – 4pm \nBRN and BREG Core \nRegister Here!\nIt’s a tough life for a plant: make dinner\, create and nurture offspring\, fight off predators\, deal with the neighbors. In Beginning Botany we’ll explore how plants handle these daily challenges using and modifying only leaves\, stems\, and roots. We’ll cover the basics of plant structure and function. \nAlexandra Holland has a passion for getting people excited about the natural world through classes\, hikes\, and photography.  She graduated from Duke University and earned her master’s degree in botany from the University of Texas at Austin.  While in Texas\, Alexandra managed the UTEX Culture Collection of Algae at UT Austin and volunteered with education programs at the Lady Bird Johnson Wildflower Center.  Upon moving to Asheville\, she began volunteering with the NC Arboretum’s youth education programs.  In 2008 she was in the first class of students to be certified as Blue Ridge Naturalists.   Alexandra teaches botany classes at the NC Arboretum and leads nature hikes in Western NC for groups of all ages. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/beg-botany-nov-26/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BREG,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs-46.jpg
END:VEVENT
