SUMMARY:Jackson Grimm's Old Time Machine
DESCRIPTION:\nJackson Grimm marries folk pop melodies with the lonesome sou
 nd of traditional Appalachian music. \n\n\n\nHis Appalachian-infused Ameri
 cana songs run the gamut from a traditional country waltz homage ("If Not 
 For You") to an unrequited love song driven by a&nbsp\;Beatles-esque melod
 y&nbsp\;("I'd Hold You\, But I Don't Wanna Hold You)" to a drunken Old Cro
 w Medicine Show-style partygrass number ("Last Train Home").\n\n\n\nGrimm 
 studied Traditonal Music at Warren Wilson College under the tutelage of re
 nowned players like Wayne Erbsen and Kevin Kehrberg. He also studied guita
 r\, banjo\, mandolin &amp\; singing&nbsp\;with the Western North Carolina 
 music master\, Josh Goforth.\n\n\n\nHe also plays extensively as a sideman
  for his father\, singer-songwriter Tim Grimm\, touring all over the US an
 d to Europe. Jackson has appeared on\, written songs on\, and co-produced 
 the last two Tim Grimm albums.&nbsp\;He's&nbsp\;has also shared the stage 
 and played with singer-songwriters Ben Bedford\, Krista Detor\, Jennie DeV
 oe &amp\; Old Sap.\n\n\n\nStill a hometown boy\, Grimm can be found playin
 g solo or around Western North Carolina with&nbsp\;Holler Choir\, One Stri
 ngband\, or his Old Time Machine.\n\n\n\nMusic 8:30-11:30pm\, $10 cover at
  the door.\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/24cT03q0IT8\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.
 be/Lu8H1TbBxaQ\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/0_4HeoySPyw\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/05/Jacksongrimm1.jpeg
END:VEVENT
