UID:27939cfe835bc3fa18461e450540c0de@ashevillechamber.org
DESCRIPTION:The words we use about ourselves and our teams aren't just des
 criptive. They're directive. Neuroscience shows that the language we repea
 t shapes the neural pathways we default to\, which means the “script” 
 a leader runs in their head (and the one they reinforce in others) can eit
 her lock in old limitations or open the door to growth. In this interactiv
 e 40-minute session\, participants will learn how identity-based language 
 patterns drive behavior\, decision-making\, and team culture\, and walk aw
 ay 
